                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8609aa45-1862-45e6-9b17-eb6665abde62",
                        "entry_id": "c5bb3f91-8eb0-3da3-9c63-1b77fc3a93ed",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "dippier"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "0f5dea64-0e2d-40a3-bf6a-d96b156cb0c8",
                        "entry_id": "c5bb3f91-8eb0-3da3-9c63-1b77fc3a93ed",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "dippiest"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa38fb63-3af5-3c72-9798-50a81d3594fe",
                        "entry_id": "c5bb3f91-8eb0-3da3-9c63-1b77fc3a93ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lacking common sense."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cdd496f-4e32-4201-9e0d-3193aa91fd81",
                                "sense_id": "fa38fb63-3af5-3c72-9798-50a81d3594fe",
                                "text": "If a person were to wash only one side of his face and continually neglect the other side, he would soon become a local curiosity–would be considered dippy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16db7832-e916-4be1-9f2f-dd53ea3c7d80",
                                "sense_id": "fa38fb63-3af5-3c72-9798-50a81d3594fe",
                                "text": "“He’s dippy,” she informed him. “Absolutely mad. He’ll wreck your ship for you.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0d0b8e4-e6ee-4a03-9ca7-2f5bd324835c",
                                "sense_id": "fa38fb63-3af5-3c72-9798-50a81d3594fe",
                                "text": "2001, Peter Bradshaw, Review of Legally Blonde, The Guardian, 26 October, 2001,\nThis so-so comedy has Witherspoon as the dippy-yet-smart sorority girl whose ambitious Wasp boyfriend dumps her because she’s a natural blonde, and he’s looking to marry “Jackie not Marilyn”; so she gets a place in his class at Harvard law school to win him back."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "77109c05-d8c8-3442-96d3-6c242a8f6e80",
                        "entry_id": "c5bb3f91-8eb0-3da3-9c63-1b77fc3a93ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having romantic feelings for; excited or enthusiastic about."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8cabda39-7987-4f6e-b601-969b66c1bf20",
                                "sense_id": "77109c05-d8c8-3442-96d3-6c242a8f6e80",
                                "text": "“I’ve read in the papers that ye’re dippy about secon’-hand stuff,” she teased, referring to his mania for antiques […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ac660a8-d157-4693-94d3-74e9f3d9782c",
                                "sense_id": "77109c05-d8c8-3442-96d3-6c242a8f6e80",
                                "text": "‘[…] If you’re dippy about a girl, and another fellow has grabbed her, it can’t be pleasant to sit at a writing table, probably with a rotten pen, sweating away while the other fellow dictates “My own comma precious darling period I worship you comma I adore you period How I wish comma my dearest comma that I could press you to my bosom and cover your lovely face with burning kisses exclamation mark”. […]’"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7fdfd709-af7c-3863-b9c1-1fd64fcf284a",
                        "entry_id": "c5bb3f91-8eb0-3da3-9c63-1b77fc3a93ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of an egg: cooked so that the yolk remains runny and can be used for dipping."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "873fceb0-ae34-4bc1-9fc3-fb9acbcd6dac",
                                "sense_id": "7fdfd709-af7c-3863-b9c1-1fd64fcf284a",
                                "text": "The flat was his domain until ten a.m., he informed her brusquely. He liked reading the paper and partaking of a dippy egg in solitude."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9cb8e577-dfd2-3f8d-bfd7-b0a7cb302a40",
                        "entry_id": "c5bb3f91-8eb0-3da3-9c63-1b77fc3a93ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Involving or suited to dipping."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ecd5a605-5656-4dee-b252-dda56bbdc5fa",
                                "sense_id": "9cb8e577-dfd2-3f8d-bfd7-b0a7cb302a40",
                                "text": "Also, salad dressing makes a great dippy sauce. Avoid low-fat salad dressings, which are usually loaded with fillers, sugar, and sodium."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb48695a-c7bd-3150-bc0a-f3381dbc089b",
                        "entry_id": "c5bb3f91-8eb0-3da3-9c63-1b77fc3a93ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having dips (downward and upward slopes)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0452376a-b068-4278-bfaa-b1d808de3c08",
                                "sense_id": "eb48695a-c7bd-3150-bc0a-f3381dbc089b",
                                "text": "\"It's not completely flat,\" Waddicor points out. \"It's a bit up and down dippy. The gradients are quite steep compared with traditional lines.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
